  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent pathway linking the compound to CD276 antigen through Caspase-5, which is targeted by multiple agents, including flavipin, isotorachrysone-6-O-alpha-D-ribofuranoside, and (+)-Menthol. All three agents share a common target, Caspase-5, and each of them has a direct interaction with CD276 antigen. This suggests that the compound may exert its effect via a mechanism that involves Caspase-5, potentially through a common pathway or a different molecular mechanism. The presence of multiple agents targeting Caspase-5 and their shared effect on CD276 antigen implies that the compound may act through a pathway that involves Caspase-5, possibly by modulating its activity or by inducing its expression. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that the compound may interact with CD276 antigen through a mechanism involving Caspase-5, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
